Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:41:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(audit): optional separate ntfy topic for audit
 checkpoints (#302)

Add `[audit] checkpoint_ntfy = { url, topic, token_file }`. When set,
kharond publishes every signed checkpoint to that topic, with its own
bearer token, and nothing else goes there; approval prompts and panic
notices stay on `[approval].ntfy`. Unset keeps the single-topic
behavior. The checkpoint keeper can then subscribe read-only to the
checkpoint topic without seeing approve/deny links.

- Config: the topic is checked with `validate_ntfy_topic` at load
  (`invalid_ntfy_topic`, so `--check` catches it), the url like
  `[approval].ntfy`'s; unknown and inline-secret keys are refused.
  The checkpoint topic alone satisfies the off-host rule.
  `checkpoint_ntfy` with `checkpoint_local_only = true` is refused
  (`audit_checkpoint_ntfy_with_local_only`), and naming the approval
  topic itself warns.
- Daemon: `Config::checkpoint_ntfy()` picks the sink topic; the token
  file is read eagerly via `NtfyTransport::new`, so a missing,
  unreadable or empty one refuses startup
  (`audit_checkpoint_sink_setup`) with no fallback.
- Docs: deployment guide "A separate checkpoint topic", runbook step
  11 (and 12), secrets inventory and warnings, example config.
- Tests: config validation, bad-config table rows, and a daemon test
  with two stub ntfy servers proving the routing and fail-closed start.

Closes #302

